  m_Name: Blade23
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Blade (8)
  description: The Blade (8) plays a vital role in the jet engine's turbine section,
    where it extracts energy from the hot gases and converts it into mechanical energy
    to drive the engine's compressor. Its position and shape are carefully designed
    to minimize energy losses and maximize airflow, making it an essential component
    of the engine's efficiency. Notably, the Blade (8) is often coated with a thin
    layer of protective material to reduce wear and tear from the high-velocity gases
    flowing over it, ensuring a long and reliable service life.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f27d028c4d88b2b4d8680253fb0eb15b, type: 3}
